  s = |S|/N = 0.001000: one off-line pair with |F(rho)|^2 = 312.923 N L^2, values (a,-a), matches S1 and S2 exactly; Delta/(N L^2) = 625.845
PASS: for every s>0 a configuration with |S| = sN reproduces the CGG values of S1 and S2.
      Hence inf |S|/N = 0 over configurations consistent with S1, S2 and with any count
      bound on off-line zeros (the construction uses a single pair).
  With the convexity-type pointwise bound |F(rho)|^2 <= T^{1/2+theta+eps}, the energy
  0.04 N L^2 ~ T L^3 needs about T^{1/2-theta-eps} off-line pairs; Selberg's density bound
  N(sigma,T) << T^{1-(sigma-1/2)/4} log T excludes only zeros with beta-1/2 >= 4(1/2+theta) > 1.

